== Spell Tier Upgrades ==

'''Reagents:''' Any spell that uses reagents has a 10% chance to not consume the reagent per spell rank.

=== Buffs ===
* -4% Cast Time
* -2% Mana Cost
* +10% Duration

=== Debuffs ===
* -4% Cast Time
* -4% Mana Cost
* +10% Duration
* -15 Resist

=== Direct Damage ===
* -2% Cast Time
* -2% Mana Cost
* -X% Reuse
* +6% Damage
* -15 Resist

=== Heals ===
* -4% Cast Time
* -2% Mana Cost
* +3% Healing

=== Damage/Healing Over Time ===
* -4% Cast Time
* -2% Mana Cost
* +5% Duration
* +3% Damage/Healing
* -15 Resist

=== Combat Innates (Proc buffs) ===
* -2% Cast Time
* -2% Mana Cost
* -X% Reuse
* +10%? Duration
* +1/2 Spell Rank to Proc

For example, [[Spirit of the Puma]] at +10 procs a +5 version of its Direct Damage proc, giving it +30% damage and -75 Resist.

=== Summon Items ===
* -? Cast Time
* -? Mana Cost
* +1 Tier Rank to item summoned

=== Crowd Control ===
Applies to Charm, Fear, Lull/Pacify, Mez, Root, and Stun spells

* -2% Cast Time
* -2% Mana Cost
* +5-10%? Duration
* +1? Level Cap
* -15 Resist

=== Dispel Magic ===
* -2% Cast Time?
* -2% Mana Cost?
* +1/2 Spell Casting Level

=== Pets ===
* -? Cast Time
* -? Mana Cost
* Pet level increased +1 (max pet level = Character Level)
* Benefits per pet level:
** +6% Hit Points
** +5 points to skills
** +1 unarmed damage (a pet that normally hits for a max of 18 will instead hit for a max of 20)
** Spells available for spell casting pets is adjusted by the pet's level

